IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`
IMPORT `sgba-versions-acts`
IMPORT `sgba-versions-later`

-- Tests for sgba-versions-later.l4. Every expected value is written from the text of the amending Act or Order and of the Revised Editions (BA1994.20030731.txt, BA1994.20120831.txt), not from what the code computed.
-- Days: Act 10 of 2005 s 32 in operation 16 February 2005 (S 76/2005, published that day); Act 22 of 2016 s 93 in operation 1 October 2016 (S 461/2016, published 29 September 2016);
-- Act 25 of 2021 s 84 in operation 1 April 2022 (published day assumed to be that day); Act 31 of 2022 s 23(1) in operation 1 November 2022 (S 850/2022, published 31 October 2022); S 26/2022 para 3 in operation 13 January 2022 (published 12 January 2022).

§ `The days`

#ASSERT `S 76/2005 was first published on` EQUALS (Date 16 2 2005)
#ASSERT `Act 10 of 2005 section 32 takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 16 2 2005)
#ASSERT `S 461/2016 was first published on` EQUALS (Date 29 9 2016)
#ASSERT `Act 22 of 2016 section 93 takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 1 10 2016)
#ASSERT `Act 25 of 2021 section 84 takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 1 4 2022)
#ASSERT `S 250/2022 was first published on` EQUALS (Date 31 3 2022)
#ASSERT `S 850/2022 was first published on` EQUALS (Date 31 10 2022)
#ASSERT `Act 31 of 2022 section 23(1) takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 1 11 2022)
#ASSERT `S 26/2022 was first published on` EQUALS (Date 12 1 2022)
#ASSERT `S 26/2022 paragraph 3 takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 13 1 2022)

§ `Which text each table reads`

#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 26 versions` (Date 15 2 2005) (Date 1 6 2006) EQUALS "s 26 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003 (31 July 2003): subsection (2) leaves a telecommunication system licensed under s 5 of the Telecommunications Act out; no power to direct co-operation with a telecommunication licensee"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the s 26 versions` (Date 16 2 2005) (Date 16 2 2005) EQUALS "s 26 as substituted by Act 10 of 2005 s 32, in operation 16 February 2005 by S 76/2005: subsection (1) excludes a telecommunication system licensed under s 5; subsection (2) is a power to direct co-operation with a telecommunication licensee"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the Act 22 of 2016 versions` (Date 30 9 2016) (Date 1 6 2020) EQUALS "as printed in the Revised Edition 2012 (31 August 2012)"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the Act 22 of 2016 versions` (Date 1 10 2016) (Date 29 9 2016) EQUALS "as amended by Act 22 of 2016 s 93, in operation 1 October 2016 by S 461/2016"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the Act 25 of 2021 versions` (Date 31 3 2022) (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS "as printed in the Revised Edition 2012 (31 August 2012)"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the Act 25 of 2021 versions` (Date 1 4 2022) (Date 1 4 2022) EQUALS "as amended by Act 25 of 2021 s 84, in operation 1 April 2022"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the Act 31 of 2022 versions` (Date 31 10 2022) (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS "as printed in the Revised Edition 2012 (31 August 2012)"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the Act 31 of 2022 versions` (Date 1 11 2022) (Date 31 10 2022) EQUALS "as amended by Act 31 of 2022 s 23(1), in operation 1 November 2022 by S 850/2022"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the S 26/2022 versions` (Date 12 1 2022) (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS "the Act without the provisions S 26/2022 inserts (the Revised Editions 2003 and 2012 do not have them)"
#ASSERT `the source of the provision text version read` `the S 26/2022 versions` (Date 13 1 2022) (Date 12 1 2022) EQUALS "the Act with the provisions S 26/2022 para 3 inserts (ss 32(2), 34(2) and (3), 35(3A) and (6), 36(3A) and (4A), 37(3), 40(3), 44(1A) and (4)), in operation 13 January 2022"
-- The rows, by name: the days each takes effect and is published.
#ASSERT `s 26 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003`'s `takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 31 7 2003)
#ASSERT `s 26 as printed in the Revised Edition 2003`'s `published on` EQUALS (Date 31 7 2003)
#ASSERT `s 26 as substituted by the Telecommunications (Amendment) Act 2005`'s `takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 16 2 2005)
#ASSERT `s 26 as substituted by the Telecommunications (Amendment) Act 2005`'s `published on` EQUALS (Date 16 2 2005)
#ASSERT `the Act 22 of 2016 wording`'s `takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 1 10 2016)
#ASSERT `the Act 22 of 2016 wording`'s `published on` EQUALS (Date 29 9 2016)
#ASSERT `the Act without the provisions S 26/2022 inserts`'s `takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 31 7 2003)
#ASSERT `the Act without the provisions S 26/2022 inserts`'s `published on` EQUALS (Date 31 7 2003)
#ASSERT `the Act with the provisions S 26/2022 inserts`'s `takes effect on` EQUALS (Date 13 1 2022)
#ASSERT `the Act with the provisions S 26/2022 inserts`'s `published on` EQUALS (Date 12 1 2022)

§ `Act 10 of 2005: section 26`

-- Argument order of (1): conduct day; reading day; the person is a broadcasting licensee or a broadcasting apparatus licensee; the facility is a telecommunication system licensed under s 5 of the Telecommunications Act.
-- before 16 February 2005: a licensee, a facility that is not a telecommunication system licensed under s 5
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the Authority may direct the licensee to share facilities, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2004) (Date 1 6 2004) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- subsection (2) of the 2003 text leaves such a system out
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the Authority may direct the licensee to share facilities, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2004) (Date 1 6 2004) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- from 16 February 2005
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the Authority may direct the licensee to share facilities, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2006) (Date 1 6 2006) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- subsection (1) now says so itself
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the Authority may direct the licensee to share facilities, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2006) (Date 1 6 2006) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a licensee
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the Authority may direct the licensee to share facilities, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2006) (Date 1 6 2006) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- before the Revised Edition 2003
#ASSERT `s 26(1) the Authority may direct the licensee to share facilities, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 30 7 2003) (Date 1 6 2006) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Argument order of (2): conduct day; reading day; the Authority is of the view that co-ordination and co-operation is necessary for the provision of a broadcasting service.
-- before 16 February 2005 there was no such power
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the Authority may direct the broadcasting licensee to cooperate with the telecommunication licensee, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2004) (Date 1 6 2004) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- from 16 February 2005
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the Authority may direct the broadcasting licensee to cooperate with the telecommunication licensee, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2006) (Date 1 6 2006) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- without the Authority's view that it is necessary
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the Authority may direct the broadcasting licensee to cooperate with the telecommunication licensee, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2006) (Date 1 6 2006) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the day it takes effect, read on the day S 76/2005 was published
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the Authority may direct the broadcasting licensee to cooperate with the telecommunication licensee, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 16 2 2005) (Date 16 2 2005) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- read the day before
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the Authority may direct the broadcasting licensee to cooperate with the telecommunication licensee, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 16 2 2005) (Date 15 2 2005) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the day before it takes effect
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the Authority may direct the broadcasting licensee to cooperate with the telecommunication licensee, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 15 2 2005) (Date 1 6 2006) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- after the day the sources were last checked
#ASSERT `s 26(2) the Authority may direct the broadcasting licensee to cooperate with the telecommunication licensee, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 5 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

