#ASSERT `s 8(5) and (6) are part of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- before the Revised Edition 2003
#ASSERT `s 8(5) and (6) are part of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 30 7 2003) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 
#ASSERT `s 8(5) and (6) are part of the Act, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 5 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Subsection (5), argument order: conduct day; reading day; the Authority has required a charge, of the amount it determined, for the late payment.
-- before 1 April 2024 there was no such power
#ASSERT `s 8(5) the licensee must pay the late payment charge, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2020) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- from 1 April 2024
#ASSERT `s 8(5) the licensee must pay the late payment charge, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no charge required
#ASSERT `s 8(5) the licensee must pay the late payment charge, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 
#ASSERT `s 8(5) the licensee must pay the late payment charge, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 5 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Subsection (6), argument order: conduct day; reading day; the day the amount was collected. It answers only where subsection (6) is part of the Act on the reading.
-- collected long before 1 April 2024
#ASSERT `s 8(6) the amount is deemed always to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings lie, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) (Date 18 3 2008) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the day before the commencement
#ASSERT `s 8(6) the amount is deemed always to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings lie, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) (Date 31 3 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the day of the commencement: not "before" it
#ASSERT `s 8(6) the amount is deemed always to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings lie, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) (Date 1 4 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
-- collected after the commencement
#ASSERT `s 8(6) the amount is deemed always to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings lie, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 4 11 2026) (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- subsection (6) is not yet part of the Act
#ASSERT `s 8(6) the amount is deemed always to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings lie, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2020) (Date 1 6 2020) (Date 18 3 2008) EQUALS NOTHING
-- read the day before S 244/2024 was published
#ASSERT `s 8(6) the amount is deemed always to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings lie, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 4 2024) (Date 27 3 2024) (Date 18 3 2008) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the day it takes effect, read on the day S 244/2024 was published
#ASSERT `s 8(6) the amount is deemed always to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings lie, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 4 2024) (Date 28 3 2024) (Date 18 3 2008) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- read after the day the sources were last checked
#ASSERT `s 8(6) the amount is deemed always to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings lie, for conduct on a day, the law read as at a day` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 5 11 2026) (Date 18 3 2008) EQUALS NOTHING

